      "source_id": "nikl-chinese-diaspora-name-guidance",
      "answer_date": "2026-03-23",
      "finding": "No clearly defined separate transcription rule for overseas Chinese names. In absence of one, use the person’s actual language and pronunciation; consider how the person or close associates say the name. Chinese versus Malay/Indonesian transcription may differ.",
      "body_capture_id": "nikl-chinese-diaspora-name-guidance"
    },
    {
      "source_id": "nikl-simplified-traditional-guidance",
      "answer_date": "2025-12-15",
      "finding": "NIKL does not separately regulate character script choice. Its dictionaries use traditional Chinese forms for Chinese place names, but that editorial practice is not a mandatory rule.",
      "body_capture_id": "nikl-simplified-traditional-guidance"
    },
    {
      "source_id": "nikl-chinese-phonology-guidance",
      "answer_date": "2026-08-14",
      "finding": "The six initials ㄐ, ㄓ, ㄗ, ㄑ, ㄔ, ㄘ are represented as ㅈ, ㅉ, ㅊ; after these, the specific medial sequence ㅑ, ㅖ, ㅛ, ㅠ is written ㅏ, ㅔ, ㅗ, ㅜ.",
      "body_capture_id": "nikl-chinese-phonology-guidance"
    }
