  "conservative_use_limits": [
    "This is a contemporary-Mandarin reading rule: apply it only after a reliable source confirms that the person uses Mandarin and provides or validates Hanyu Pinyin.",
    "English spelling alone is not sufficient to identify Hanyu Pinyin versus Wade-Giles or another romanization. Ambiguous forms such as Chun/Chung remain on hold until pinyin and reading are independently verified.",
    "The mapping cases above are direct table entries or explicitly identified component compositions; they are not a general surname dictionary and do not decide published/conventional-name status.",
    "The Chinese diaspora guidance means the Mandarin table must not be applied mechanically to a Chinese-heritage person who uses another language or pronunciation."
  ],
